## The correction made for the seven differences (issue 111)

The seven differences named above were the port's own success-envelope suffix
on the unsubscribe link, and nothing else. The link now carries the
reference's bytes in every configuration: the reference's view posts no
success envelope, so the port posts none either
(src/card/notify/follow-mail-views.ts).

The seven historically affected steps are replayed step for step on the
committed synthetic-v1 deck and the mail the engine sends is compared byte
for byte with the fixture's recorded Ruby answer
(tests/card/notify/notification-unfollow-link-parity.test.ts): all seven
failed before the change with exactly the suffix above, and all seven pass
after it.

That test is a targeted check of those seven recorded answers. It is NOT a
current grade of the synthetic-v1 fixture: the tallies above belong to their
own historical run, and a fresh admitted comparison of the whole fixture is
still required before any current verdict is assigned.
